extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 18: Mystic Russia pp.59-61, read from the text layer. IMPORTED UNDER D4. NO xp_table, per D3. THE BOOK PRINTS ''Dowsing'' IN THE PSIONICS LINE AND PALLADIUM HAS NO SUCH PSIONIC POWER: checked against the live catalog''s 116 psionic rows (nothing matching under any spelling), against Rifts Ultimate Edition printed 306 where Dowsing is a WILDERNESS SKILL, and against Palladium Fantasy printed 221 and 229 where it is a LEVEL ONE EARTH WARLOCK INVOCATION costing 2 P.P.E. The catalog holds all three of those readings - a Dowsing skill, Earth: Dowsing and Water: Dowsing, and an unprefixed shaman Dowsing from Spirit West - and none of them is a psionic power. It is therefore NOT granted, in either block: adding it to magic.spells would move it out of the block the book put it in, and inventing a psionic row would invent a power Palladium does not print. The other five psi-powers are granted as printed. ''ALL SUMMONING SPELLS INVOLVING ANIMALS'' is enumerated as the three general invocations that summon and command animals - Animals, Canines, Rodents. Summon Game Animals is deliberately excluded: it carries tradition ''shaman'' and belongs to Spirit West, not to the general invocation list a Rifts Russia entry reaches. Summon & Control Sea Serpents is excluded as a monster rather than an animal, and as nothing a forest spirit commands. THE BOOK SEPARATES ''Natural Abilities'' FROM ''R.C.C. Skills'' AND THIS IMPORT KEEPS THAT SEAM: prowl, climb, swim and the tracking percentages are printed under Natural Abilities and are recorded there rather than granted as catalog skills. ''all animal, farm and plant lore'' has no clean landing: the catalog holds one Lore: Cattle & Animals row (filed under Cowboy, covering the animal and farm halves) and no plant lore at all, so Identify Plants & Fruit carries the third. The +35% is for SELECTED skills only - the book says ''all selected skills'', where the Domovoi says ''all get'' - so the named skills sit at their printed or catalog figures. The text layer carries this book''s digit cipher: the M.D.C. line prints ''+4D4xlO'' and the P.P.E. line ''!D4xlOO''."
