# Leshii

## Lore

A ten-foot forest giant with the legs and cloven hooves of a goat, shaggy from
head to toe, with a human face, a long pointed beard, short thick horns and
glowing red eyes. It moves through the forest as quietly as a mouse and holds
complete reign over the animals in it.

Most Leshii are good natured and have a wonderful sense of humour, which almost
nobody else appreciates. They see themselves as the protectors of the forest,
and reserve their wrath for people who waste it: polluters, lumbermen who cut
without conservation, sportsmen who kill for fun, and anyone bringing unnatural
forces onto the land.

Even then it prefers to chase rather than kill - leading pursuers in circles for
hours until they arrive back where they started, smashing traps, freeing
animals, hiding equipment high in trees, leading people into bogs. Like the
Domovoi it is protective of children and will guide a lost one home.

## Alignment

Any, but the majority are unprincipled (40%) or anarchist (30%).

## GM Notes

**It will never accept or use modern weapons or technology.** That is the
book''s own wording and it is the hardest line any Woodland Spirit here draws -
harder than the Domovoi''s simple disinterest. A Leshii in a party is a
ten-foot creature carrying a tree.

It has no love for demons, witches or necromancers and will join forces to rid
a forest of them, which is what makes it playable at all. But grasslands are
too open, cities are horrid, and most humans regard even a heroic Leshii as a
dangerous animal that might pounce at any moment.

**The book lists Dowsing among its psionics.** Dowsing is not a psionic power
anywhere in Palladium - it is an Earth Warlock invocation and a Wilderness
skill - so it is not granted here in either block. See `extraction_notes`.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'leshii');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'leshii';

